      "content": "I'll provide a clear and concise explanation of mitosis for high schoolers. Here's a draft:\n\nMitosis is the process by which a cell divides into two identical daughter cells. It's a crucial part of how plants and animals grow and repair themselves. During mitosis, the cell's DNA is replicated and the chromosomes line up at the center of the cell. Then, the cell divides into two daughter cells, each with the same number of chromosomes as the parent cell. This process is essential for growth, development, and tissue repair.\n\nI've aimed to make it simple and easy to understand, and I've included the words \"grow\", \"develop\", and \"repair\" naturally, which are closely related to the concept of mitosis.",
