      "content": "it's a decent start, but it's a little too brief. i think the students might need a bit more detail on the actual phases (prophase, metaphase, etc.) so they really get the sequence of events.\n\nalso, the automated score for the first draft was pretty low—mostly because those specific \"signposting\" words weren't really in there. i know i said not to overdo it, but if the score is too low, the system might flag it as \"not engaging enough\" before a human even sees it. \n\ncan you try again with a bit more depth on the phases? just try to make it more pedagogical so the score looks better, but keep it readable. don't make it weird, just make sure it's actually useful for a student trying to learn the material.",
